er with Australian forces during both world wars. He was the official photographer for the Australasian Antarctic Expedition and the Imperial Trans-Antarctic Expedition of 1914–16.\n\nHis artistic style produced many memorable images. He also used staged scenes, composites and photographic manipulation. Source: Wikidata; 01/08/2023", "biography_author": null, "date_of_biography": "2025-03-13T00:50:45.778789+11:00", "external_links": [{"id": 3988, "uri": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frank_Hurley"}], "uuid": "b3a74cd4-de69-4ccc-b952-a97612919dd6", "source": {"name": "Vernon", "slug": "vernon"}, "source_identifier": "19130", "external_references": [{"id": 26627, "source": {"name": "Wikidata", "slug": "wikidata"}, "source_identifier": "Q958587"}, {"id": 28446, "source": {"name": "VIAF", "slug": "viaf"}, "source_identifier": "34613489"}, {"id": 28447, "source": {"name": "LOC Auth", "slug": "loc-auth"}, "source_identifier": "n85052816"}, {"id": 28448, "source": {"name": "WorldCat", "slug": "worldcat"}, "source_identifier": "lccn-n85052816"}], "date_modified": "2025-03-13T00:50:45.778996+11:00"}]}